From 22a690e7f34ca240dffb0933bcf81bd8698694b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:50:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add Rack::TempfileReaper to the endpoint middleware stack

Multipart uploads parsed by Rack::Multipart create tempfiles that were
left open on disk after the request unless the host app (e.g. Rails)
already ran Rack::TempfileReaper. Use it in every endpoint's stack so
they are closed and unlinked once the response body is closed.

Fixes #2487
---
 CHANGELOG.md                        |  1 +
 lib/grape/endpoint.rb               |  1 +
 spec/grape/integration/rack_spec.rb | 40 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 42 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 034d240..4c46e89 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 * [#3008](https://github.com/ruby-grape/grape/pull/3008): Add the grape-on-rack app as a live-server memory profiling harness - [@ericproulx](https://github.com/ericproulx).
 * [#3025](https://github.com/ruby-grape/grape/pull/3025): Add `:md` and `:markdown` formatters that render an object's `to_markdown`, for APIs that declare a `text/markdown` content type - [@ericproulx](https://github.com/ericproulx).
 * [#3029](https://github.com/ruby-grape/grape/pull/3029): Add a built-in `:jsonl` (JSON Lines) format that streams an Enumerator body - [@ericproulx](https://github.com/ericproulx).
+* [#XXXX](https://github.com/ruby-grape/grape/pull/XXXX): Add `Rack::TempfileReaper` to every endpoint's middleware stack so multipart upload tempfiles are unlinked after the response - [@anyingiit](https://github.com/anyingiit).
 * Your contribution here.
 
 #### Fixes
diff --git a/lib/grape/endpoint.rb b/lib/grape/endpoint.rb
index fd68663..96f0c2c 100644
--- a/lib/grape/endpoint.rb
+++ b/lib/grape/endpoint.rb
@@ -462,6 +462,7 @@ module Grape
       content_types = setting.content_types
       format = setting.format
 
+      stack.use Rack::TempfileReaper
       stack.use Rack::Head
       stack.use Grape::Middleware::Error, **error_middleware_options(format, content_types)
 
diff --git a/spec/grape/integration/rack_spec.rb b/spec/grape/integration/rack_spec.rb
index 174da58..e39d191 100644
--- a/spec/grape/integration/rack_spec.rb
+++ b/spec/grape/integration/rack_spec.rb
@@ -50,6 +50,46 @@ describe Rack do
     end
   end
 
+  # https://github.com/ruby-grape/grape/issues/2487
+  describe 'multipart tempfiles' do
+    let(:uploaded_paths) { [] }
+
+    let(:app) do
+      paths = uploaded_paths
+      Class.new(Grape::API) do
+        params do
+          requires :file, type: File
+        end
+
+        post 'upload' do
+          paths << params[:file][:tempfile].path
+          'ok'
+        end
+
+        post 'failed_upload' do
+          paths << params[:file][:tempfile].path
+          error!('failed', 422)
+        end
+      end
+    end
+
+    let(:upload) { Rack::Test::UploadedFile.new(__FILE__, 'text/plain') }
+
+    it 'unlinks the tempfile once the response is closed' do
+      post '/upload', file: upload
+      expect(last_response.body).to eq('ok')
+      expect(uploaded_paths.size).to eq(1)
+      expect(File.exist?(uploaded_paths.first)).to be(false)
+    end
+
+    it 'unlinks the tempfile when the endpoint returns an error' do
+      post '/failed_upload', file: upload
+      expect(last_response.status).to eq(422)
+      expect(uploaded_paths.size).to eq(1)
+      expect(File.exist?(uploaded_paths.first)).to be(false)
+    end
+  end
+
   context 'when the app is mounted' do
     let(:ping_mount) do
       Class.new(Grape::API) do
